      "revision": 1368771662,
      "text": "Chrysalidocarpus tsaravoasira is a species of flowering plant in the Arecaceae family. It is a palm endemic to Madagascar, where it grows in lowland and lower montane rain forests up from 40 to 1,200 meters elevation. There are perhaps 500 plants remaining, and the population is decreasing due to overharvest."
